  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the man as 'me' in the text",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the man (with beard and crossed arms) because the text explicitly uses 'me' to refer to the speaker. The man is visually mapped as 'me' in the text, creating a direct semiotic projection where the viewer identifies with the speaker. The text 'thank you for allowing me into your country' and 'now we need to talk about the things that need to change around here to accommodate my beliefs' directly addresses the viewer ('you') and refers to the speaker ('me'), which is visually embodied by the man. The user is thus projected onto the man as the 'me' in the text.",
